     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p3-theory",
     "replacement": "- **Related rates of change problems** link the rates of change, with respect to time $t$, of two related variables such as $x$ and $y$.\n- Use the **chain rule** to connect these rates.\n\n1. Identify the 3 variables.\n2. Set up the chain rule.\n3. Differentiate and substitute the given rate.\n4. Evaluate at the given variable value.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p3-theory",
     "targetFingerprint": "c6c01f66be53f0904c9920ebabb693685a2dd2811c29d3c7358da885f36d46ce",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6ext1-2-further-rates-of-change-v1/20261111-122539",
   "revision": 21
  },
  "c7a000dc-2296-416b-b852-41cf952d1c75": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p28-introduction",
     "replacement": "In **modified growth and decay** models, the rate of change of a quantity $Q$ is proportional to the difference between $Q$ and a constant value $P$, so $\\dfrac{dQ}{dt}=k(Q-P)$ for a constant $k$.\n\nThe larger the difference, the faster the change.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p28-introduction",
     "targetFingerprint": "87cbaaa71ac569e963857950ffe90183d08b0386e78fb2060b9e5c321fcaf9ce",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6ext1-2-further-rates-of-change-v1/20261111-122539",
   "revision": 21
  },
